      "description": "Three element forms at once, all hard-edged and all the same white: closed spirals of about two turns, one to each major muscle mass; long shallow arcs following the contour of the zone they sit in; and fields of short dashes lying parallel to the nearest arc, in broken tracks. The dashes crowd along the topline and the back edges of the shoulder and hindquarter and thin to isolated marks at the belly. The two sides are not mirrored, and the spirals do not all turn the same way. Nothing on the head, nothing below the knee.",
